<title>CANADA: Western Canada rail car allocations for Sept 22.</title>
<headline>Western Canada rail car allocations for Sept 22.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Canada's Car Allocation Policy Group on Wednesday issued its rail car allocations by commodity for loading during shipping week nine starting Sept 22.</p>
<p>VANCOUVER     3,200 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	2,364 CWB (wheat/barley)</p>
<p>		    818 canola</p>
<p>		     18 oats</p>
<p>PRINCE RUPERT 1,200 CWB THUNDER BAY   2,600 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	1,7t8 CWB</p>
<p>		    426 canola</p>
<p>		    273 oats</p>
<p>		    153 domestic feed wheat and barley</p>
<p>CHURCHILL	 320 CWB</p>
<p>*does not include U.S.-bound rail cars or interior domestic shipments.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
